From: gsm-system compatibility maintainers
Subject: Retry transient UHD RX timeouts without accepting sample gaps

A single empty 100 ms UHD receive timeout is transient on some USB paths.
Retry up to ten consecutive waits or one second, without restarting the RF
stream or device clock. The first resumed packet must start exactly at the
previous accepted packet end so a timestamp gap cannot expose stale I/Q data.

